<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leonardo Loredan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1436">1436</a>–<a href="/years/1521">1521</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Lunardo Loredan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leonardo Loredan was a Venetian nobleman and statesman who reigned as the 75th <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/doge-of-venice">Doge of Venice</a> from 1501 until his death in 1521. Born into the noble Loredan family, he traded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a> before rising through the Republic's magistracies, among them Savio del Consiglio, podestà of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padua">Padua</a>, ducal councillor and, from 1492, Procurator of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-the-evangelist">Saint Mark</a>, one of the highest offices of the state. As doge he led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-league-of-cambrai">War of the League of Cambrai</a>, in which the Republic was defeated in 1509 before a new alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xii-of-france">Louis XII of France</a> in 1513. Under his rule, in 1516, a decree isolated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> of Venice in the first Ghetto.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leonardo-loredan.jpg" alt="Leonardo Loredan" width="330" height="463" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giovanni Bellini · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Giovanni_Bellini,_portrait_of_Doge_Leonardo_Loredan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
